B.The City agrees to match the project costs provided by WYDOT at the rate of nine
and fifty-one hundredths percent (9.51%) of the cost of right-of-way acquisition,
Exhibit B-1. The City agrees to reimburse to WYDOT any funds above those
authorized by WYDOT and matched by the City necessary to build this project.
C.
It is understood by the parties that the above-mentioned percentages may vary
slightly during the life of this Agreement, as dictated by the Federal Notices on
Sliding Scale Rates of Federal Aid Participation in Public Lands States.Itisfurther
understood by the City that the estimated costs may vary as the project plans are
developed and let to contract and that the City shall reimburse WYDOT for the
total amount not paid with federal funds.
D.
The costs shown on Exhibit B-1 are estimates only and the City understands that
the final costs may be higher or lower.Rates may vary for the life of this project
based on federal reviews and approval.If the actual costs go over the total estimated
amendment for the additional costs.
E.
The City agrees to pay their portion of actual cost of this project, including all
indirect costs through the current Indirect Cost Allocation Plan (ICAP) rate as
approved by the Federal Highway Administration (FHWA). ICAP is a rate built
intoWYDOT's accounting systemfor overhead expenditures for administering a
project.TheICAPrate is developed byWYDOT and approved by the FHWA, with
the new rate taking effect immediately. The current rate of eleven percent (11%) is
effective until September 30,2024, at whichtime the rate is subject to change based
on FHWA approval.The ICAPrate will be charged on total direct costs on this
project as shown on Exhibit B. WYDOT will bill the City on a monthly basis unless
otherwise agreed upon between the parties.
5.
Reimbursement.The Cityhereby agrees to reimburse WYDOTfor its share of actual
costs incurred to the Project, less previous payments, within forty-five (45) days after
billing pursuant to Wyo.Stat. 16-6-602.
6.
Responsibilities of City. City agrees to:
A.Reimburse WYDOT in accordance with Sections 4 and 5 above.
B.
The City shall provide WYDOT design plans for the pedestrian underpass and
associated elements by the project due dates established byWYDOT and provided
to the City in writing.
C.
Submit aletter to WY DOT designating a qualified project representative, at no cost
toWYDOT, capable of making timely decisions and authorized to sign documents
concerning the construction of the Project.
Amended and Restated Cooperative Agreement between Wyoming Department of Transportation
